<title>USA: U.S. JULY PPI ENERGY GOODS PRICES.</title>
<headline>U.S. JULY PPI ENERGY GOODS PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				July   June   July97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods     0.1    0.7     -1.4</p>
<p> -Gasoline		    -1.0    0.4     -5.7</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		 -3.4   -5.8     -6.1</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	  0.6    1.8	1.7</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				July   June   July97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods    -1.1    0.6     -3.0</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z     -3.8    1.6     -3.6</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		    -3.5    3.1     -7.4</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		 -5.0   -1.9    -12.6</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	   -6.7    3.4    -11.2</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				July   June   July97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials   -0.4   -2.9     -3.8</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			-5.0    3.0     -0.5</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z	     -2.4    3.3     -1.6</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		  6.2  -14.1     -8.3</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
